.TH NVIM-LINK-HOST 1 "2026-06-30" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvim-link-host \- print the host token used in Neovim file hyperlinks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvim-link-host
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvim-link-host
prints the host identity that terminal file hyperlinks should embed for the
current Neovim or terminal context. Consumers such as ripgrep hostname wrappers
can use the value to generate OSC-8 file links that route correctly through
termnav.
.PP
The helper has no options. It resolves context through termnav's
.B nvim-link-context
library and prints the selected host token to standard output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMNAV_REMOTE_LINK_HOST
Explicit remote host identity to use when the surrounding shell or tmux server
already knows the correct host.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A host token was printed.
.TP
.B 1
Context resolution failed.
.TP
.B 2
The helper could not resolve its installed library path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eza-nvim-links (1),
.BR nvim-tmux-open (1)
